 ## Background
-Restricted Adjacency Merging was introduced in the context of parallel isosurface extraction for very large geophysical datasets. It was developed to address load imbalance issues in distributed memory architectures (e.g., clusters managed by LSF-HPC) where the extraction time of sub-blocks varied significantly [S1, S2]. The method builds on the extended tandem algorithm and Marching Cubes isosurface extraction [S1, S2].
+Restricted Adjacency Merging was introduced in the context of parallel isosurface extraction for very large geophysical datasets [S1]. It was developed to address load imbalance issues in distributed memory architectures (e.g., clusters managed by LSF-HPC) where the extraction time of sub-blocks varied significantly [S1]. The method builds on the extended tandem algorithm and Marching Cubes isosurface extraction [S1, S2].
 
